//             '<p>Farewell Yellow Brick Road is the last ever tour for this particular megastar, bringing to a close half a century on the road for one of pop&rsquo;s most enduring artists. Beginning in the United States, the tour will take in more than 300 concerts across five continents, with performances in North America, Europe, Asia, South America, and Australia. It is a brand new &ndash; and last ever &ndash; production from Elton, who will take his fans along with him on a highly visual musical adventure spanning a peerless 50-year career that is bursting with hits.</p>\n<p><strong>News:</strong><br />Due to the Covid-19 pandemic, the event organisers and the Accor Arena announced that the Elton John concerts, initially scheduled for 10, 11, and 13 October 2020, then for 10, 12, and 13 October 2021, have been postponed until 25, 27, and 28 June 2023</p>\n<p>All existing tickets remain valid for the new dates, as follows:</p>\n<p>Tickets for the cancelled concert at 8pm on Saturday 10 October 2021 will be valid for the concert at 8pm on 25 June 2023.<br />Tickets for the cancelled concert at 7pm on Sunday 12 October 2021 will be valid for the concert at 8pm on Tuesday 27 June 2023.<br />Tickets for the cancelled concert at 8pm on Tuesday 13 October 2021 will be valid for the concert at 8pm on Wednesday 28 June 2023.</p>',
